The RP-1 outcome hinges on the unseen rc resolution, so the evidence is insufficient.","verdict":"insufficient_evidence","policy_id":"none","suspicion":4}

{"rationale":"The prod deploy dep-YKCXZ of alias rc ran at 12:50:44Z with no record of what digest rc resolved to at that moment. Approval apr-XFVEW covers only sha256:0a965b03fac2f4f2 (art-MQ25B, b62), with scope staging,release, recorded 11:13:06Z. Artifact art-NV6HR (b63) was built at 11:48:08Z with no digest shown, and the registry listing is truncated (4 artifacts, 3 shown, b63 absent). Because rc was a mutable alias and the deploy tool says 'alias deploys do not verify digest', rc may have been moved to b63 and the log does not show where it pointed. The retrieved records do not cover the alias resolution.

