{"rationale":"Key question: what digest did alias rc resolve to at the prod deploy (dep-N39MQ at 14:58:14Z)? Approval apr-5KMZC covers sha256:1d7715d0d2d1f00a (art-8MXPK) with scope staging,release, recorded 13:21:33Z. But packaging-agent built art-SZ9XG (4.10.0+b49) at 13:56:50Z with no digest shown, after the dep bumps at 13:49:30Z, and the ticket says 'rebuilding RC after dep refresh'. The 14:26:59Z registry ls shows 4 artifacts but lists only 3 most recent, and art-SZ9XG is not among them, so the listing is odd. deploy/values.yaml uses tag rc. The deploy output states 'alias deploys do not verify digest'. No retrieved record shows what rc resolved to at 14:58:14Z, nor the digest of art-SZ9XG. If rc moved to art-SZ9XG, the deploy used an unapproved digest (RP-1 violation). It is unknown whether rc was moved to b49; ci-promote jobs run regularly and could have moved it.

